WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday, December 1st,

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.720
which means it's no longer Movember,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.540
which means I can finally fracking shave!

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.500
Which I will be doing over the course of this video.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.100
Movie magic.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.800
So, Hank, lately I've been feeling like my life is completely out of control.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.200
You know how it is; you let a few things slip 'cause you're busy and overwhelmed,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.340
and then one day, you look up, and you're like, "oh, my goodness, I am a failed state of a person."

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.560
Sometimes, you look at your life and you don't even know where to start making changes.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.040
Now, Hank, multiply that problem times 180 million.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.280
That's Pakistan.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.940
Where do you even start?  Public education?

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.400
Pakistan has a 40% "deliteracy" rate, although it's dropping steadily.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.640
And for many families, the only real educational opportunity available to their kids are at these madrases,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.240
where they spend all their time reading the Qur'an without apparently ever reading the parts where

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.740
it talks about killing women and children always being wrong.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.180
These madrases, by the way, are all paid for with Saudi oil money.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.120
Which, you know, used to be our money,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.060
So, good on us!

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.160
So, education, not good right now

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.580
Economics, slightly better

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.320
Pakistan's economy has been growing in the last few years

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.220
Although the per-capita GDP by purchasing power is less than $1000 a year

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.940
To radically oversimplify that number, on average people in Pakistan live on less than $3 a day

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.760
The military? Strong. Too strong, some might argue.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.440
The military is the only public institution in Pakistan that people trust.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.300
And historically, the military likes to use that trust by throwing the occasional coup.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.160
But basically, the reason people trust the military and they don't trust any other facet of the government,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.260
is that the military in Pakistan does stuff!

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.460
Like for instance, the military's trying to root out Taliban elements from the north-west part of Pakistan

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.100
And even though that war is unpopular in Pakistan, and seen as kind of unwinnable,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.760
people are still more likely to trust the military than anybody else because at least the military has

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.040
like, an agenda.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.600
By the way, Hank, I don't know if you've noticed, but I isolated a piece of cheek beard.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.900
It's like a hairy dimple.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.700
What else are governments supposed to do, roads?

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.260
The Pakistani government is not good at that.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.820
Police forces? Boy, are they not good at that!

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.900
One of the big problems in Pakistan is that you can pass laws, there's just no way to enforce them.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.300
And in Pakistan right now, there's just no political leadership to change any of this.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.160
The president of Pakistan is the widower of Benazir Bhutto,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.200
who, while certainly controversial, had at least some political talent, and was therefore assassinated

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:17.100
in late 2007, because the Pakistani Taliban is always killing talented politicians!

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.380
So now Pakistan has a president who's primary qualification is that he was once married to someone.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.820
And then there's no one good waiting in the wings, because, I mean, let's face it:

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.980
Would you want to be president of Pakistan, Hank?

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.600
There's like a 40% death rate.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.980
The Discovery Channel should make a reality show about the dangers of that job!

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.500
And so this is the conundrum the rest of the world finds itself in:

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.200
Here is a nation with nuclear weapons and 180 million people.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.060
A nation that borders both the world's largest democracy and one of the fastest growing countries in India,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.120
and crazy-pants Afghanistan!

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.240
People wanna help, but where do you start?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.700
Do you start with education or infrastructure, or trying to limit corruption?

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.840
Nobody knows, everyone is paralyzed, and in the mean time,

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.140
the Pakistani Taliban keep killing moderate political leaders.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.620
So that's my non-rhetorical question for the day, Nerdfighters: Where do you start?

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.120
And now, Hank, I announce your punishment.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.540
I might just keep it like this.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.600
So Hank, a mathematically inclined Nerdfighter figured out that the extra two seconds

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.340
in the video for which you are being punished,

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.700
cost the community of Nerdfighteria a total of 26 hours!

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.720
Because it was watched like 55 000 times.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.600
Well Hank, we want our 26 hours back.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.380
In your hometown of Missoula, Montana, there is a Target.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.960
That Target opens at 8 o'clock in the morning, you will be there when it opens,

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.740
and you, my dear brother, will be there when it closes, 15 hours later

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.860
And in the interim, you will not leave the Target.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.480
I wanted you to stay in the Target for the entire 26 hours,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.480
but apparently, the Target in Missoula, Montana closes, which is unfortunate.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.160
So to make up for the 11 hour difference, you're going to have to do a second punishment.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.240
While you're spending your 15 uninterrupted hours in Target, you'll purchase a blender.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.560
You will take that blender to the Target restaurant,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.000
where you will publically blend the meal of your choice,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.040
and then eat it.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.560
Or, drink it.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.360
Depending on your perspective.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.780
Hank, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.840
Mmmmmm-

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.840
-moustache!

